WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:04.640
Rhiannon: When a child’s behaviour seems
different from his or her peers, there

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.060
may be concerns that, “something is wrong
with them.” Although children develop at

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:13.569
different rates, a clinical assessment
from a professional and possibly some

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:15.660
early intervention, can be helpful.

00:00:16.779 --> 00:00:21.330
As they get older, the question of a
mental health diagnosis may come up

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.960
because a child or adolescent who has
been progressing fine, suddenly becomes

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.430
very angry, sad, or worried all the time.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.610
Leah: There are no definitive
medical tests to detect whether

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:36.339
someone has a mental health disorder
such as a blood test or scan.

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:37.252
Mental health diagnoses are based on
clinical interviews, observations,

00:00:37.252 --> 00:00:37.255
and sometimes tasks and tests
the child is asked to complete.

00:00:37.255 --> 00:00:37.267
The positives of having a mental
health diagnosis are that it gives

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:50.175
access to specialised services and
can help by giving the problem a name.

00:00:50.175 --> 00:00:58.840
By giving it a name, it means someone
has seen it before, they are not alone,

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:03.060
and information can be shared with
others experiencing similar problems.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.920
Rhiannon: By having a name, it also makes
it easier to explain the issues to others

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:12.949
and maybe access specific help as the
illness becomes the problem not the child.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:17.869
Mental health diagnoses can be
presented as a fixed part of a

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:21.910
person, but it is also important
to consider that things change over

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:26.700
time and a mental health diagnosis
is not always a diagnosis for life.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.910
Leah: There are also alternatives
to having a mental health diagnosis.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:34.780
Mental health professionals may
work to understand the problem in

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.620
the child or young person’s family,
social and educational context,

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:42.990
without necessarily feeling the
need to give a formal diagnosis.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.580
Rhiannon: They may also look at
what is the overall problem that is

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:50.539
creating the mental health issues,
and how does the child’s interactions

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.020
with others effect the problem?

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:56.860
Clinical interventions and strategies
can be used with both parents and

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:04.689
children without the need for a formal
diagnosis, and a diagnosis is not always

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:07.370
necessary to access therapy or support.

